<title>USA: Deutsche says pleased with its Italy business.</title>
<headline>Deutsche says pleased with its Italy business.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Deutsche Bank AG said it was pleased with its activities in Italy and that whether or not Italy joined European monetary union would make no difference to its operations there.</p>
<p>The bank's chief executive Hilmar Kopper told a news conference in Washington, &quot;In Italy we are very satisified. This is is absolutely irrespective of whether Italy will join or will not join monetary union&quot;.</p>
<p>The fact that Deutsche had continued to step up its presence in the Italian market was proof that it was pleased with its operations there, he added.</p>
</text>
